  ],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "Now let's translate that proof directly into code.",
      "start_ms": 0,
      "end_ms": 4120,
      "start_frame": 0,
      "end_frame": 124,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "First, store n, then transpose the matrix.",
      "start_ms": 4360,
      "end_ms": 7880,
      "start_frame": 131,
      "end_frame": 236,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "For each row, r, we do not start column C from 0.",
      "start_ms": 8240,
      "end_ms": 13640,
      "start_frame": 247,
      "end_frame": 409,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "Instead, C starts from r plus 1.",
      "start_ms": 14120,
      "end_ms": 17120,
      "start_frame": 424,
      "end_frame": 514,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Why?",
      "start_ms": 17660,
      "end_ms": 17960,
      "start_frame": 530,
      "end_frame": 539,
      "word_count": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Because we only need one side of the main diagonal.",
      "start_ms": 17980,
      "end_ms": 21340,
      "start_frame": 539,
      "end_frame": 640,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Suppose we swapped row 0, column 1 with row 1, column 0.",
      "start_ms": 22440,
      "end_ms": 28360,
      "start_frame": 673,
      "end_frame": 851,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "If we later reached row 1, column 0, and swap them again, we would undo our own work.",
      "start_ms": 28840,
      "end_ms": 36700,
      "start_frame": 865,
      "end_frame": 1101,
      "word_count": 18
    },
    {
      "text": "So each pair must be processed exactly once.",
      "start_ms": 37140,
      "end_ms": 41260,
      "start_frame": 1114,
      "end_frame": 1238,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "That is why for row r, column begins at r plus 1.",
      "start_ms": 41960,
      "end_ms": 46220,
      "start_frame": 1259,
      "end_frame": 1387,
      "word_count": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "For each such pair, swap matrix with matrix.",
      "start_ms": 46640,
      "end_ms": 51120,
      "start_frame": 1399,
      "end_frame": 1534,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "When those loops finish, the matrix is transposed.",
      "start_ms": 52420,
      "end_ms": 55740,
      "start_frame": 1573,
      "end_frame": 1672,
      "word_count": 8
    },
    {
      "text": "Then the second step is very small.",
      "start_ms": 55740,
      "end_ms": 59340,
      "start_frame": 1672,
      "end_frame": 1780,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "For every row, reverse that row.",
      "start_ms": 59700,
      "end_ms": 61980,
      "start_frame": 1791,
      "end_frame": 1859,
      "word_count": 6
    },
    {
      "text": "That is the complete solution.",
      "start_ms": 62480,
      "end_ms": 63940,
      "start_frame": 1874,
      "end_frame": 1918,
      "word_count": 5
    },
    {
      "text": "Transpose, then reverse rows.",
      "start_ms": 64580,
      "end_ms": 66200,
      "start_frame": 1937,
      "end_frame": 1986,
      "word_count": 4
    },
    {
      "text": "Now, complexity.",
      "start_ms": 66840,
      "end_ms": 68100,
      "start_frame": 2005,
      "end_frame": 2043,
      "word_count": 2
    },
    {
      "text": "The transpose processes roughly half of the n by n matrix.",
      "start_ms": 68780,
      "end_ms": 73040,
      "start_frame": 2063,
      "end_frame": 2191,
      "word_count": 11
    },
    {
      "text": "That is still O of n squared.",
      "start_ms": 73500,
      "end_ms": 75820,
      "start_frame": 2205,
      "end_frame": 2275,
      "word_count": 7
    },
    {
      "text": "Reversing all rows also processes n squared values overall.",
      "start_ms": 76500,
      "end_ms": 81140,
      "start_frame": 2295,
      "end_frame": 2434,
      "word_count": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "So together, the total time remains O of n squared.",
      "start_ms": 81460,
      "end_ms": 85980,
      "start_frame": 2444,
      "end_frame": 2579,
      "word_count": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "And because both transformations happen inside the original matrix, the extra space is O of 1.",
      "start_ms": 86460,
      "end_ms": 95240,
      "start_frame": 2594,
      "end_frame": 2857,
      "word_count": 16
    },
    {
      "text": "This gives us a clean, optimal, in -place solution.",
      "start_ms": 96060,
      "end_ms": 100860,
      "start_frame": 2882,
      "end_frame": 3026,
      "word_count": 9
    }
  ],
